WEBVTT

00:00.940 --> 00:07.612
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.940 --> 00:07.612
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.676 --> 00:14.703
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.676 --> 00:14.703
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.288 --> 00:21.960
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.288 --> 00:21.960
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.985 --> 00:28.199
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.985 --> 00:28.199
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.093 --> 00:34.765
This surging power...

00:29.093 --> 00:34.765
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.093 --> 00:31.180
Black Jack

00:36.267 --> 00:42.522
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.267 --> 00:42.522
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.316 --> 00:48.278
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.316 --> 00:48.278
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.849 --> 00:57.204
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.849 --> 00:57.204
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.705 --> 00:59.396
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.396 --> 01:01.389
will be there

01:01.409 --> 01:04.369
It makes me glad...

01:01.409 --> 01:04.369
yokatta

01:04.614 --> 01:12.094
That I found my place here.

01:04.614 --> 01:12.094
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.147 --> 01:13.665
Oh WISDOM

01:13.665 --> 01:15.514
will be there

01:15.542 --> 01:18.183
I searched for the reason

01:15.542 --> 01:18.183
sagashita

01:18.184 --> 01:25.232
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.184 --> 01:25.232
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.817 --> 01:32.697
as long as we're alive.

01:25.817 --> 01:32.697
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.698 --> 01:34.783
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.867 --> 01:37.051
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.203 --> 01:39.814
His name is Black Jack.

02:00.393 --> 02:03.228
Why are you barking so much in the morning, Largo?

02:07.650 --> 02:09.651
What the heck are you doing?

02:18.263 --> 02:19.263
Pinoco!

02:20.437 --> 02:21.562
Doc!

02:21.706 --> 02:24.753
Do you like how nice your room looks with all the pretty flowers?

02:24.917 --> 02:25.834
Clean them up.

02:26.950 --> 02:28.297
Get rid of all of them.

02:28.379 --> 02:30.213
Are you trying to turn this house into a flower shop?

02:30.214 --> 02:33.235
Don't take flowers from the wild
just because they're pretty!

02:33.551 --> 02:34.509
They're alive too!

02:37.867 --> 02:39.103
You dummy!

02:39.140 --> 02:42.262
I made so many trips to carry all of them in!

02:46.567 --> 02:49.482
Originally "Arranging Life” by Tezuka Osamu

02:46.567 --> 02:49.482
Arranging the Flower of Life

02:52.653 --> 02:54.905
Sheesh, Doc!

02:54.906 --> 02:56.637
You carried all of those?

02:56.866 --> 02:58.533
And it wasn't easy!

02:59.118 --> 03:01.953
Doc must not like flowers!

03:02.121 --> 03:05.290
But I've never seen anyone who didn't like flowers.

03:05.291 --> 03:06.750
Right? Right?

03:06.751 --> 03:08.729
I love flowers too.

03:08.983 --> 03:09.983
Cheer up.

03:10.296 --> 03:12.672
Say, do you want to go see this?

03:11.989 --> 03:12.622
Ikebana Art Exhibit

03:13.623 --> 03:14.990
An ikebana art exhibit?

03:15.043 --> 03:16.706
What is ikebana?

03:16.719 --> 03:23.793
It is believed that ikebana was started in the sixth century
by Buddhist monks who were arranging flowers to...

03:25.227 --> 03:28.063
It's the art of arranging flowers so they look pretty.

03:29.565 --> 03:31.524
Art of flower arranging?

03:34.738 --> 03:36.525
30th annual Eiko school
Ikebana Exhibit

03:41.869 --> 03:44.107
Here and there. Flowers everywhere!

03:44.205 --> 03:46.706
And they're all wonderful.

03:46.707 --> 03:47.540
Yeah.

03:48.501 --> 03:49.487
What's over there?

03:50.419 --> 03:52.072
Excuse me here.

03:58.315 --> 03:59.928
It's really pretty.

03:59.962 --> 04:01.002
It really is.

04:01.055 --> 04:03.442
It was arranged by the daughter of the head of the school.

04:03.648 --> 04:06.893
But I wonder why she wouldn't make a public appearance?

04:07.135 --> 04:09.268
I hear she's ill.

04:09.382 --> 04:10.275
Is that so?

04:10.582 --> 04:11.650
Poor thing.

04:11.776 --> 04:12.587
Honma-kun.

04:13.142 --> 04:14.142
Mr. Baba!

04:14.482 --> 04:16.482
This is my ikebana instructor.

04:16.502 --> 04:17.609
Nice to meet you.

04:17.622 --> 04:18.743
Nice to meet you too.

04:19.448 --> 04:23.243
Honma-kun, your father is a renowned surgeon, if I recall?

04:23.917 --> 04:24.382
Yes.

04:24.620 --> 04:27.706
But he passed away three years ago.

04:27.991 --> 04:28.957
Really?

04:29.333 --> 04:33.586
The head of the Eiko school asked
me to find a skilled surgeon.

04:33.587 --> 04:35.297
That's why I was looking for you.

04:35.343 --> 04:36.603
I know of one.

04:37.300 --> 04:41.428
He's a surgical genius-matched by no one.

04:41.429 --> 04:42.408
Right?

04:41.790 --> 04:42.368
Yup.

04:42.680 --> 04:45.348
But the fee will be very expensive.

04:46.225 --> 04:47.907
Better be prepared.

04:53.858 --> 04:55.692
Doc, look, look!

04:55.693 --> 04:56.985
All the flowers!

05:07.788 --> 05:09.622
It's a big mansion.

05:10.041 --> 05:10.540
Let's go.

05:10.541 --> 05:11.281
Yes.

05:19.976 --> 05:20.689
It's bitter!

05:20.749 --> 05:22.726
It's not yummy at all.

05:22.842 --> 05:24.909
This is the taste of green tea.

05:24.942 --> 05:27.151
But the sweets look delicious.

05:28.389 --> 05:29.626
Yum!

05:29.643 --> 05:32.395
I'll eat yours too if you aren't eating them!

05:32.396 --> 05:34.272
Hey! Pinoco! Those are mine!

05:35.731 --> 05:36.970
Pinoco! Why you...

05:38.152 --> 05:39.736
Thanks for waiting for us.

05:40.529 --> 05:43.907
I am the assistant to the head of the
Eiko School of Ikebana, Kiyota.

05:45.367 --> 05:46.451
And this is the seventeenth head.

05:46.452 --> 05:48.620
And this is the seventeenth head.

05:48.621 --> 05:50.163
I am Eiko Seisui.

05:50.456 --> 05:53.375
Thank you very much for coming.

05:54.355 --> 05:55.715
Nice to meet you.

05:57.046 --> 06:02.467
The person I would like you to
examine is my daughter, Sono.

06:02.968 --> 06:04.719
She has a troublesome disease.

06:04.720 --> 06:08.515
She has been told she may not live to be twenty.

06:08.516 --> 06:10.350
She's nineteen right now.

06:10.351 --> 06:14.395
Every doctor so far has told us that she can
live for a few more months at the most.

06:16.899 --> 06:19.526
She's sensitive to light.

06:19.527 --> 06:22.529
When exposed to sunlight, her skin inflames,

06:22.530 --> 06:25.281
and her life shortens.

06:25.282 --> 06:28.576
So I've never allowed her to go outside.

06:29.203 --> 06:31.371
She can't play outside?

06:31.539 --> 06:32.414
That's right.

06:37.086 --> 06:39.275
Not only can she not step outside,

06:39.362 --> 06:41.842
but I've also isolated her from
contact with the outside world.

06:43.050 --> 06:44.777
Sono, we're coming in.

06:44.927 --> 06:45.552
OK.

06:56.897 --> 06:58.982
She's really pretty.

06:59.275 --> 07:02.612
Sono, this is Dr. Black Jack.

07:02.902 --> 07:04.697
Yes, so I've heard.

07:05.448 --> 07:07.740
Let's begin the checkup.

07:22.173 --> 07:26.009
I'm sorry, but she can live for a few more months at best.

07:26.010 --> 07:27.635
I know that.

07:27.825 --> 07:33.600
What I want is for you to prolong her life for a year.

07:34.143 --> 07:34.767
For a year?

07:34.768 --> 07:35.602
Yes.

07:35.603 --> 07:39.564
We have an evaluation to determine the
new head of the Eiko school in a year.

07:39.797 --> 07:43.049
I really want her to be selected.

07:43.050 --> 07:45.844
She has the talent for it.

07:45.845 --> 07:46.936
Kiyota.

07:47.721 --> 07:50.723
Please allow me to present this to you.

07:50.724 --> 07:53.726
One, ten, a hundred, a thousand...

07:53.727 --> 07:54.644
¥500,000,000?!

07:54.645 --> 07:56.938
Ohmigewdness!

07:56.939 --> 07:59.357
If that's not enough, I'll pay you ¥1,000,000,000.

07:59.358 --> 08:00.900
Or even ¥2,000,000,000!

08:01.402 --> 08:02.628
Are you serious?

08:03.028 --> 08:05.445
She'll die soon after, even if she
is chosen to be the new head.

08:06.449 --> 08:08.224
I'm very serious.

08:08.451 --> 08:11.494
I want to make her the head of the school.

08:11.495 --> 08:15.123
I want her to enjoy the glory of
it, even if for but a moment.

08:15.124 --> 08:16.124
One year!

08:16.125 --> 08:17.542
One year is all I ask!

08:17.543 --> 08:21.555
Doctor, please prolong her life!

08:24.967 --> 08:27.135
Doc, what are you going to do?

08:34.602 --> 08:36.176
That is superb.

08:36.437 --> 08:40.482
But there are many other candidates
who are better than you.

08:40.483 --> 08:42.901
Upon succession to the position of the head of the school,

08:42.902 --> 08:46.000
you must create a masterpiece on the spot.

08:46.572 --> 08:51.701
Do you want people to laugh at the work of the new head?

08:52.703 --> 08:55.163
If you want to avoid such shame, improve your skills.

08:55.307 --> 08:57.900
Now, arrange them again.

08:58.334 --> 08:58.956
Yes.

09:06.175 --> 09:07.509
Largo, next.

09:11.722 --> 09:13.806
Doc! Look, look!

09:13.998 --> 09:15.058
What's that?

09:15.059 --> 09:17.477
I've decided to do ikebana too.

09:18.270 --> 09:22.148
This.is my first.piece, a Maiden's Prayer,.

09:22.525 --> 09:26.528
Rather than a Maiden's Prayer, it looks
like it should be called a Maiden's Cry.

09:26.529 --> 09:28.429
There are too many flowers.

09:29.657 --> 09:32.825
You just don't understand the artistry of it.

09:37.576 --> 09:38.036
Yes.

09:38.249 --> 09:39.958
Doctor, she's...

09:40.167 --> 09:41.209
Sono-sama is...

09:45.172 --> 09:46.548
She's stable for now,

09:46.966 --> 09:48.675
but she's not doing well.

09:48.676 --> 09:49.592
No way...

09:52.054 --> 09:55.139
You're making her work too hard, aren't you?

09:55.140 --> 09:58.393
It's all to let her acquire adequate enough skills to
be worthy of becoming the head of the school.

09:58.394 --> 10:00.144
It will all be meaningless if she dies!

10:00.145 --> 10:03.690
It will all be meaningless if she can't
become the head of the school.

10:03.691 --> 10:07.110
So, Doctor, you will perform the operation, right?

10:07.403 --> 10:10.071
I don't perform meaningless operations.

10:10.447 --> 10:12.101
It won't be meaningless!

10:12.241 --> 10:17.120
Once she becomes the head of the school, her name
will be part of the history of the Eiko school forever.

10:17.121 --> 10:18.756
Please, Doctor!

10:22.710 --> 10:24.833
Sono-tan, are you OK?

10:26.213 --> 10:27.880
You should be resting!

10:28.507 --> 10:31.742
I must arrange some flowers.

10:32.094 --> 10:33.344
I don't have any time.,

10:33.345 --> 10:35.178
B-But...

10:35.238 --> 10:36.157
It's OK.

10:36.181 --> 10:38.683
I can tell I won't live for long.

10:38.684 --> 10:39.267
So...

10:39.268 --> 10:40.435
Sono-tan...

10:40.644 --> 10:42.323
So I must arrange some flowers.

10:42.604 --> 10:45.724
So I can become the head of the
school while I'm still alive.

10:46.233 --> 10:47.233
That's...

10:47.234 --> 10:49.319
That's my destiny.

10:54.158 --> 10:56.534
Is this Valkyrie Hospital in Germany?

10:57.202 --> 10:59.454
I have a question I'd like to ask.

10:59.955 --> 11:00.496
Yes.

11:30.762 --> 11:33.044
Excuse me!

11:34.683 --> 11:37.518
What's the purpose of today's visit?

11:37.519 --> 11:38.728
It's a secret.

11:38.854 --> 11:40.229
I see.

11:40.230 --> 11:41.230
You see?

11:51.825 --> 11:53.701
Miss, you have a guest.

11:55.080 --> 11:56.898
Hello, Sono-tan.

11:57.084 --> 11:58.557
I came to visit you.

11:58.630 --> 11:59.825
Pinoco-chan.

12:00.292 --> 12:02.001
You should be lying down.

12:02.137 --> 12:04.712
I'm sorry, but I'm feeling well today.

12:05.237 --> 12:08.519
I have a present for you.

12:10.552 --> 12:15.640
They were blooming so beautifully in the field,
so I thought you might want to arrange them.

12:15.766 --> 12:16.098
Here.

12:16.569 --> 12:17.725
Dandelions...

12:17.726 --> 12:18.951
I haven't seen them in a while.

12:19.269 --> 12:22.480
But dandelions are seldomly used in ikebana.

12:22.678 --> 12:23.958
They're no good?

12:24.131 --> 12:25.131
I'm sorry.

12:25.158 --> 12:26.795
Did you hear that?

12:27.069 --> 12:29.478
I'll take you back to the field.

12:29.655 --> 12:30.530
Right.

12:30.531 --> 12:33.033
Then they can continue to bloom beautif...

12:39.998 --> 12:41.165
Sono-tan?

12:41.166 --> 12:44.659
Pinoco-chan, I've forgotten something
very important until now!

12:45.212 --> 12:46.483
Flowers are alive.

12:46.922 --> 12:49.298
After seeing only cut flowers for so long,

12:49.299 --> 12:53.825
I've been treating them as if they were materials.

12:54.304 --> 12:56.264
Thank you, Pinoco-chan!

13:10.487 --> 13:13.823
<i>They were blooming so beautifully in the field...</i>

13:19.329 --> 13:22.415
Miss, breakfast is ready.

13:23.208 --> 13:24.125
Miss?

13:26.089 --> 13:26.838
Miss!

13:27.082 --> 13:27.622
Someone!

13:27.689 --> 13:28.342
She's missing!

13:44.605 --> 13:46.221
These are wildflowers!

13:46.565 --> 13:50.487
These are flowers' true forms.

13:51.486 --> 13:55.448
They're so pretty, yet full of life.

13:56.597 --> 13:57.597
I...

13:58.044 --> 13:59.044
I...

14:10.422 --> 14:12.006
Sono-tan!

14:12.007 --> 14:16.052
We found her in the field up on the hill and...

14:16.064 --> 14:17.404
How could that be?!

14:17.477 --> 14:18.843
Keep it quiet for a minute!

14:20.933 --> 14:23.142
Doctor, I...

14:23.143 --> 14:24.960
Are you trying to kill yourself?

14:25.354 --> 14:27.941
You know full well what kind of condition you have!

14:28.065 --> 14:29.716
I'm sorry, Doctor.

14:30.150 --> 14:34.904
But I really wanted to see some wildflowers.

14:35.139 --> 14:36.322
Sono-tan...

14:36.323 --> 14:37.406
They were beautiful.

14:37.950 --> 14:40.076
They were glowing to their fullest.

14:40.577 --> 14:43.891
I thought to myself, “If only I could put these in a vase.”

14:44.081 --> 14:45.581
That's it, Sono!

14:45.582 --> 14:47.750
That's the spirit of ikebana!

14:47.751 --> 14:49.669
Kiyota, prepare some flowers immediately!

14:49.670 --> 14:50.252
Yes!

14:50.671 --> 14:52.129
Enough already!

14:53.090 --> 14:56.184
Is ikebana the only thing you can think about?!

14:56.510 --> 14:59.136
She could have been dead by now!

14:59.137 --> 15:03.099
Doctor, I'll die soon anyway, right?

15:03.100 --> 15:03.724
Then...

15:04.175 --> 15:05.577
Why do you assume that?!

15:06.019 --> 15:08.839
I've seen many patients who were worse off than you.

15:09.106 --> 15:10.940
Pinoco was one of them!

15:13.986 --> 15:17.149
When she came to me, she was in no condition to survive.

15:17.656 --> 15:20.157
If things hadn't gone well, she may not be here today.

15:20.575 --> 15:22.986
But she tried to live.

15:23.578 --> 15:25.077
She wanted to live!

15:25.664 --> 15:29.500
It's that desire that made her live up until now.

15:29.501 --> 15:30.295
She's alive!

15:31.461 --> 15:33.546
Pinoco-chan was?

15:33.880 --> 15:37.545
People and flowers are both beautiful
because they're trying to live.

15:37.843 --> 15:39.520
I don't believe a person

15:39.636 --> 15:41.846
who's given up the will to live would be able

15:41.847 --> 15:43.219
to produce something that speaks
to other people's hearts.

15:43.515 --> 15:46.016
Doctor! Please wait!

15:46.059 --> 15:47.101
Doctor!

15:56.438 --> 16:00.674
<i>People and flowers are both beautiful
because they're trying to live.</i>

16:05.704 --> 16:09.498
Let it have the glow the wildflowers had.

16:14.447 --> 16:14.897
Yes.

16:14.921 --> 16:17.506
Doctor, Sono has...

16:20.927 --> 16:23.220
Doctor, finally...

16:23.597 --> 16:25.222
Finally she's done it!

16:25.223 --> 16:31.687
Sono has created a masterpiece that the
Eiko school can truly be proud of.

16:32.689 --> 16:35.981
Doctor, I want to live.

16:36.087 --> 16:36.747
Sono!

16:36.827 --> 16:37.827
Sono-tan!

16:38.236 --> 16:42.071
I want to keep living, like these flowers,

16:42.282 --> 16:43.282
and like Pinoco-chan.

16:43.650 --> 16:45.910
Please work on me,

16:45.911 --> 16:49.431
so I can live a day or even an hour longer.

16:52.959 --> 16:53.876
Doctor...

16:55.545 --> 16:56.462
OK.

16:59.674 --> 17:00.925
Pinoco, let's get started.

17:00.926 --> 17:02.676
Aye-aye!

17:04.054 --> 17:04.846
Scalpel.

17:08.436 --> 17:09.576
Miss...

17:09.856 --> 17:10.898
Sono...

17:19.194 --> 17:21.487
<i>Sono-tan, hang in there.</i>

17:25.784 --> 17:26.242
Clamp.

17:26.243 --> 17:27.201
Here.

17:27.202 --> 17:28.327
Administer the vasopressor.

17:28.328 --> 17:29.078
Yes.

17:30.747 --> 17:31.705
Blood pressure?

17:31.706 --> 17:33.207
120/64.

17:33.208 --> 17:34.875
She's doing fine.

17:34.876 --> 17:35.584
Good.

17:35.669 --> 17:36.669
We're almost done.

17:36.670 --> 17:37.294
Hang in there.

17:43.760 --> 17:45.085
Suture complete.

17:45.387 --> 17:47.012
This concludes the operation.

17:50.976 --> 17:52.523
D-Doctor!

17:52.855 --> 17:53.936
It's done.

17:53.937 --> 17:54.937
The operation was a success.

17:58.998 --> 18:00.180
Really?!

18:00.245 --> 18:01.525
Thank you ver...

18:11.174 --> 18:13.209
The Head of the Eiko School
Succession Ceremony

18:13.448 --> 18:16.500
Doc! There it is!

18:16.501 --> 18:17.418
Doctor, Pinoco-chan.

18:17.494 --> 18:18.586
Hello there.

18:18.587 --> 18:21.853
The-head of the school was very happy you helped them.

18:22.132 --> 18:23.382
I'm so happy for them.

18:23.383 --> 18:28.762
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you all for coming today.

18:28.889 --> 18:32.850
We will announce who the new head
of the Elko school will be today..

18:32.851 --> 18:35.134
Her name is Eiko Sono.

18:35.353 --> 18:38.939
The entire board has approved of her talent.

18:38.940 --> 18:41.993
Please give her your blessings.

18:45.864 --> 18:47.497
She's so pretty.

18:47.699 --> 18:49.450
I've never seen her before.

18:49.451 --> 18:50.784
She's very beautiful.

18:50.827 --> 18:51.660
She's like...

18:51.661 --> 18:53.871
She's like a nymph among flowers.

18:55.582 --> 18:58.500
Sono-tan is really beautiful.

18:58.960 --> 19:02.755
Please enjoy a demonstration by
the new head of the school.

19:18.974 --> 19:19.974
Miss...

19:20.023 --> 19:21.899
Sono, that's magnificent.

19:35.080 --> 19:35.996
Is that...

19:36.081 --> 19:37.206
A dandelion?

19:50.637 --> 19:51.893
Sono-tan...

19:59.938 --> 20:00.813
Doctor!

20:01.898 --> 20:02.986
Sono-tan!

20:03.483 --> 20:05.526
Thank you so much, Doctor.

20:05.527 --> 20:10.864
She's blossomed nicely into the head of the school.

20:11.324 --> 20:12.866
Congratulations, Sono-san.

20:12.867 --> 20:14.910
Sono-tan, you were beautiful!

20:14.911 --> 20:16.495
And that dandelion was really nice!

20:16.496 --> 20:18.122
And that dandelion was really nice!

20:18.623 --> 20:20.144
It's all because of you.

20:20.458 --> 20:23.085
You are like my master.

20:23.086 --> 20:24.683
Oh, no...

20:25.922 --> 20:27.840
Doctor, I'm sorry for the delay until now,

20:27.841 --> 20:29.888
but here is the fee, as promised.

20:30.302 --> 20:32.803
I'm amazed that you're willing to spend
such a large sum of money.

20:32.928 --> 20:34.455
Oh no.

20:34.639 --> 20:37.300
Even if she is to depart from this world,

20:37.600 --> 20:43.897
this one day of glory is priceless to us.

20:43.922 --> 20:45.275
Right, Sono?

20:45.308 --> 20:45.981
Yes.

20:46.795 --> 20:48.042
One day...

20:48.320 --> 20:51.155
No, you might enjoy it for another fifty years.

20:53.613 --> 20:55.426
F-Fifty years?

20:55.869 --> 20:57.911
I performed that kind of operation.

20:57.912 --> 21:01.195
I told you I hate performing meaningless operations.

21:01.541 --> 21:05.544
I had to buy information from all over the world, so it cost quite a bit though.

21:05.545 --> 21:07.796
So, Sono will...

21:08.256 --> 21:10.424
There shouldn't be anything to worry about.

21:10.425 --> 21:12.551
See you again, Sono-tan.

21:12.552 --> 21:14.261
Wait up, Doc!

21:16.829 --> 21:17.829
Father!

21:18.099 --> 21:19.142
Sono!

21:20.675 --> 21:23.108
Forgive me, Sono.

21:23.313 --> 21:29.431
I wanted you to leave proof that you lived
by becoming the head of the Eiko school.

21:29.694 --> 21:32.112
That's why I treated you so harshly.

21:32.113 --> 21:34.573
I knew that.

21:34.574 --> 21:36.241
Thank you, Father.

21:37.118 --> 21:38.087
Thank you.

21:46.861 --> 21:48.837
They're really pretty.

21:48.838 --> 21:49.630
Yeah.

21:50.382 --> 21:53.801
I love wildflowers the best.

21:54.260 --> 21:56.261
Yeah, me too!

21:56.679 --> 21:59.765
Keep blooming all you can, everyone.

22:10.547 --> 22:17.553
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.547 --> 22:17.553
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.554 --> 22:24.726
Only look straight at me.

22:17.554 --> 22:24.726
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.771 --> 22:32.028
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.771 --> 22:32.028
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:32.029 --> 22:42.538
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:32.029 --> 22:42.538
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.539 --> 22:47.919
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.539 --> 22:47.919
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.920 --> 22:57.303
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.920 --> 22:53.125
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.580 --> 22:57.304
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.304 --> 23:08.064
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.304 --> 23:08.064
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.065 --> 23:13.152
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.065 --> 23:13.152
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.153 --> 23:26.123
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.153 --> 23:26.123
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.124 --> 23:33.047
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.124 --> 23:33.047
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:33.048 --> 23:43.933
just as it was lead by the light.

23:33.048 --> 23:36.981
sora no hate tooku

23:37.074 --> 23:43.874
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.102 --> 24:15.037
An Operation in a Thunderstorm

23:45.102 --> 23:46.462
They're closed...

23:46.275 --> 23:46.775
Jeez!

23:46.855 --> 23:47.895
He's in serious condition.

23:48.915 --> 23:50.355
Well kid, I'm off.

23:50.375 --> 23:51.635
Doc, you dummy!

23:52.668 --> 23:54.355
I'm sorry, Mom.

23:54.462 --> 23:57.595
I'm tired of living.

23:58.021 --> 23:59.522
I don't want to do this job.

23:59.823 --> 24:02.110
Doctors are all lying crooks!

24:02.276 --> 24:03.956
Kiddo, let's make a deal.

24:04.036 --> 24:05.902
You're such a dirty scumbag!

24:05.959 --> 24:06.612
Shut up!

24:06.646 --> 24:10.642
I'll pay ¥50,000,000 to the person
who can save Dad.

24:11.343 --> 24:14.243
Next Karte - An Operation in a Thunderstorm.

24:16.174 --> 24:17.754
Karte NG...

24:19.011 --> 24:21.496
I brought you a present.

24:21.680 --> 24:22.638
Ta-da!

24:23.443 --> 24:24.697
Oh no!
